			"File": [
				"⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				1939,
				1
			],
			"Message": "docs(Wind): Update documented workspace path to .fiddee directory\n\nThe inline comment in ResolveConfiguration referencing `~/.land/workspaces/RecentlyOpened.json` as the source for the `?folder=` URL parameter was stale after the product was rebranded to FIDDEE. Update the path to `~/.fiddee/workspaces/RecentlyOpened.json` to reflect the current Mountain data directory.\n\nNo behavior change — the comment is documentation-only.",
			"SHA": "e601d9150381470501bc44c54689c6cdc868b8d4"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-05-19T22:22:26Z",
			"File": [
				"⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				1939,
				1
			],
			"Message": "fix(Wind): Add __TAURI_INTERNALS__ invoke fallback and robust path defaults\n\nResolveConfiguration attempts to access the Tauri IPC bridge via (window as any).__TAURI__.core?.invoke, which is undefined in Tauri v2 webview contexts where the API lives under __TAURI_INTERNALS__ instead. Add __TAURI_INTERNALS__?.invoke to the fallback chain before the __TAURI__ variants so the invoke lookup succeeds regardless of which Tauri version provides it.\n\nReplace all || undefined path fallbacks (homeDir, tmpDir, userDataDir, logsPath) with concrete string defaults. VS Code's AbstractNativeEnvironmentService wraps these with URI.file() and path.join(userDataDir, 'User'); if any value is undefined, path.posix.join(undefined, 'User') throws \"The path argument must be of type string\" during workbench open(). Emitting fallback paths (/tmp, /tmp/.fiddee) lets the workbench boot in degraded mode when Mountain IPC fails rather than hard-crashing in initServices.\n\nAlso propagate the fallback pattern to extensionsPath, constructing it from userDataDir or its /tmp/.fiddee default so extension scanning never receives undefined.",
			"SHA": "6c4941e7097cb404d47ae6b26e0241313731012d"
		}
	],
	"TimeStamp": 1779882037449
}